rd.\" That puts him on the restrictive side. He never states rung 4's rule (teams by sex assigned at birth), and nothing he says separates rung 4 from rung 5 (a complete ban), so he can't be seated in a chair. I coded it `statement-other` because it was an interview, not a questionnaire or debate answer.\n- **Other passages:** I coded only one other source, the OnTheIssues pointer page, as `not-evidence`; it says nothing on this topic. I gave no rows to the CNN debate, the Fresno forum or the four policy pages. None of them mentions the topic.\n- **needs_source:** his speech at the Clovis track and field championships, where he says he announced his plan, and a campaign policy page on girls' sports if one exists.\n- **Quotes:** two from the interview, both quotable and tiered `lever` with the `lever-unclear` flag. The flag is there because no other candidates' passages were supplied for the opponent test (T1), and he never names the legislation.\n\nThe GitHub plugin failed to connect, and several claude.ai connectors (Benevity, Candid, Canva, Figma, Harvey, WorkOS) need authorizing in your claude.ai connector settings. This task didn't need any of them.","ttft_ms":9629,"type":"result","duration_ms":29011,"uuid":"198d6958-6dc2-4803-9281-adce98a20bc7","ttft_stream_ms":1550,"time_to_request_ms":102,"first_content_frame_ms":1551,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
